# MOUSE: P.I. For Hire (PPSA26578) -- boot to the first gameplay scene ("Big Mouse, Little Hope").
#
# VALIDATED 2026-10-06 on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV), frontend `prosper-app`, native
# 1920x1080, PROSPER_RENDER=1, no render acceleration, twice: on `main` and on the #4609 head.
# Both reach the difficulty select by flip 1300, the intro cinematic by flip 1600 and gameplay
# by flip 2000 (144 s and 192 s into the two runs; the machine was loaded during the second).
#
# WHAT THE ROUTE HAS TO GET PAST. These are the screens seen in the captures of those runs; the
# first four come before flip 1300 and their exact order was not recorded:
#
#   logos, auto-save notice             Cross
#   LANGUAGE & SUBTITLES                Cross on NEXT
#   the agreement (around flip 900)     has to be SCROLLED to the end before NEXT accepts it
#   analytics prompt                    Cross on NEXT
#   difficulty select (flip 1300)       Cross (the first portrait is preselected)
#   intro cinematic (flip 1600)         plays through
#
# Cross every four seconds answers all of those but the agreement. For that one both sticks and
# the d-pad are held down in flip-anchored windows, and ONLY there. The menus run at 2 to 7
# flips/s, so a wall-clock window misses the screen on a loaded machine; and a version that kept
# scrolling afterwards carried the selection down the main menu and opened the credits, which
# looks like progress in a log and is not.
#
# The surplus Cross presses simply wait on whatever screen the boot is on, and in gameplay they
# are the jump button, which is harmless standing still.
#
# What a run of this route shows today is the HUD, the objective text and one lit patch of floor
# in an otherwise dark scene (tracker #4556). It is a route to the scene, not evidence that the
# scene renders.
